window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-0b1cfdb2fc517807"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"scan-multiple-repositories\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">扫描多个代码库</h1> <p>对多个代码库执行安全扫描，并检查结果与覆盖范围。</p> <p>使用 Codex Security CLI 按指定提交扫描一组代码库，逐项检查结果，并决定哪些问题需要调查或修复。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要按指定提交评估一组服务的安全团队。</li> <li>需要可重复的代码库清单和相互独立扫描结果的工程团队。</li> <li>需要跨代码库对发现和覆盖缺口进行优先级排序的审查人员。 <a id=\"related-links\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_3\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">安装并完成 CLI 身份验证</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0462b3e291010c32\">批量扫描与代码库发现</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=codex-security-bulk-scan\">批量扫描命令参考</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">开始之前</h2> <p>先完成 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/cli\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CLI 快速入门（需联网）</a>，安装并验证 Codex Security CLI 的身份。确认你有权使用安全扫描功能，并且能访问自己拥有或获准评估的代码库。扫描使用你本机已有的权限，不会暂停等待审批；请先查看<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/cli/reference#local-scan-permissions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">扫描权限说明（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-the-repository-inventory\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">准备代码库清单</h2> <p>先从少量代码库开始。将以下内容保存为 <code>repositories.csv</code>，然后替换示例 URL 和提交占位符：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-csv\">id,repository,revision\npayments,https://github.com/YOUR-ORG/payments.git,REPLACE_WITH_FULL_COMMIT_SHA\nidentity,https://github.com/YOUR-ORG/identity.git,REPLACE_WITH_FULL_COMMIT_SHA\n</code></pre> <p>为每个代码库指定唯一的 <code>id</code> 和完整提交 SHA。你可以在本地检出目录中运行以下命令获取 SHA：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">git -C /path/to/repository rev-parse HEAD\n</code></pre> <p>每次扫描都会检查对应提交的整个代码库。分支名称、缩短后的哈希和未提交变更不属于此工作流。关于文件夹范围或代码库专属指令，请参阅 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/cli/bulk-scans#create-a-repository-csv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CSV 选项（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><strong>GitHub 选项：</strong> 你也可以从自己的 GitHub 账户或组织中<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/cli/bulk-scans#discover-github-repositories\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">交互式选择代码库（需联网）</a>，而不是准备 CSV。</p> <p><a id=\"run-the-scans\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">运行扫描</h2> <p>在 <code>repositories.csv</code> 所在目录中执行命令；将输出路径替换为被扫描代码库之外的私有目录：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --workers 2 \\\n  --mode standard \\\n  --max-attempts 1 \\\n  --max-cost 5\n</code></pre> <p>这会同时运行两次标准扫描，每个代码库尝试一次。<code>--max-cost 5</code> 会在某次尝试的估算费用超过 5 美元时停止它。已在进行的工作可能会超过估算值，因此这不是硬性费用上限，也不是整个运行共享的预算。请在开始前选定这些参数。</p> <p>CLI 会把每个代码库的结果分别保存到 <code>security-scans/artifacts/</code> 下的文件夹中。请将结果保存在私有位置：其中可能包含源代码摘录和漏洞详情。</p> <p><a id=\"review-the-results\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">检查结果</h2> <p>打开结果目录并检查：</p> <ol> <li><strong>清单：</strong> 在 <code>manifest.json</code> 中确认代码库和提交。</li> <li><strong>状态：</strong> 查看每次尝试对应的 <code>results.jsonl</code>，确认状态和产物位置。</li> <li><strong>覆盖范围与发现：</strong> 在每次尝试的文件夹中查看 <code>coverage.json</code> 里的缺口与排除项，再检查 <code>report.md</code>、<code>findings.json</code> 中的发现和支持证据。</li> </ol> <p>退出码 <code>0</code> 表示每个代码库都成功完成扫描，并不表示没有漏洞。退出码 <code>2</code> 表示覆盖不完整、某个代码库未能完成，或发生输入/运行时错误。若发现列表为空但覆盖不完整，仍不能据此认定代码安全。</p> <p>为每个代码库记录下一步：调查某项发现、<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/plugin/fix-findings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">修复已确认的问题（需联网）</a>，或跟进覆盖缺口。交接给负责团队时，请注明扫描的提交和支持证据。</p> <p>要恢复中断的运行，请使用相同的 CSV、指令和输出目录重新执行同一命令。CLI 会跳过已完成的扫描，不会自动重试覆盖不完整的部分。如果要变更代码库清单、版本、范围、模式或指令，请使用新的输出目录。请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/cli/bulk-scans#resume-a-campaign\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">恢复和重试说明（需联网）</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"scan-multiple-repositories\">Scan multiple repositories</h1> <p>Run security scans across repositories and review the findings and coverage.</p> <p>Use the Codex Security CLI to scan a list of repositories at specific commits, review each result, and decide what needs investigation or a fix.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Security teams assessing a group of services at specific commits.</li> <li>Engineering teams that need a repeatable repository inventory and separate scan results.</li> <li>Reviewers prioritizing findings and coverage gaps across repositories.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">Install and authenticate the CLI</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0462b3e291010c32\">Bulk scans and repository discovery</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-909fb3f276184d34?anchor=codex-security-bulk-scan\">Bulk-scan command reference</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>Complete the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/cli\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CLI quickstart (online)</a> to install and authenticate Codex Security. Confirm that you have security scan access and Git access to the repositories you own or have permission to assess. Scans use your local permissions and don't pause for approval; review the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/cli/reference#local-scan-permissions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">scan permissions guidance (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-the-repository-inventory\">Prepare the repository inventory</h2> <p>Start with a small set of repositories. Save this as <code>repositories.csv</code>, then replace the example URLs and commit placeholders:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-csv\">id,repository,revision\npayments,https://github.com/YOUR-ORG/payments.git,REPLACE_WITH_FULL_COMMIT_SHA\nidentity,https://github.com/YOUR-ORG/identity.git,REPLACE_WITH_FULL_COMMIT_SHA\n</code></pre> <p>Give each repository a unique <code>id</code> and a full commit SHA. Get the SHA from a local checkout with:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">git -C /path/to/repository rev-parse HEAD\n</code></pre> <p>Each scan reviews that commit, including the full repository. Branch names, shortened hashes, and uncommitted changes aren't part of this workflow. For folder scopes or repository-specific instructions, see the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/cli/bulk-scans#create-a-repository-csv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CSV options (online)</a>.</p> <p><strong>GitHub option:</strong> You can <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/cli/bulk-scans#discover-github-repositories\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">choose repositories interactively (online)</a> from your GitHub account or organization instead of preparing a CSV.</p> <h2 id=\"run-the-scans\">Run the scans</h2> <p>From the directory containing <code>repositories.csv</code>, replace the output path with a private directory outside the scanned repositories, then run:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npx @openai/codex-security bulk-scan repositories.csv \\\n  --output-dir /path/outside/repositories/security-scans \\\n  --workers 2 \\\n  --mode standard \\\n  --max-attempts 1 \\\n  --max-cost 5\n</code></pre> <p>This runs two standard scans at a time, with one attempt per repository. <code>--max-cost 5</code> stops each attempt when its estimated cost exceeds $5. Work already in progress can exceed the estimate, so this is not a hard cap or a shared budget for the whole run. Choose these values before starting.</p> <p>The CLI saves each repository's results in its own folder under <code>security-scans/artifacts/</code>. Keep the results private: they can contain source excerpts and vulnerability details.</p> <h2 id=\"review-the-results\">Review the results</h2> <p>Open the results directory and check:</p> <ol> <li><strong>Inventory:</strong> Confirm the repositories and commits in <code>manifest.json</code>.</li> <li><strong>Status:</strong> Read <code>results.jsonl</code> for each attempt's status and artifact location.</li> <li><strong>Coverage and findings:</strong> In each attempt folder, read <code>coverage.json</code> for gaps and exclusions, then <code>report.md</code> and <code>findings.json</code> for findings and supporting evidence.</li> </ol> <p>Exit code <code>0</code> means every repository completed successfully, not that no vulnerabilities exist. Exit code <code>2</code> indicates incomplete coverage, a repository that couldn't complete, or an input or runtime error. An empty findings list with incomplete coverage does not establish that the code is secure.</p> <p>Record the next action for each repository: investigate a finding, <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/plugin/fix-findings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">fix an accepted finding (online)</a>, or follow up on coverage gaps. Use the scanned commit and supporting evidence when handing work to the responsible team.</p> <p>To resume an interrupted run, repeat the same command with the same CSV, instructions, and output directory. The CLI skips completed scans and does not automatically retry incomplete coverage. Use a new output directory when changing the inventory, revisions, scopes, modes, or instructions. See <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/cli/bulk-scans#resume-a-campaign\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">resume and retry guidance (online)</a> for recovery details.</p>"};
